<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>BALTAP - Mining Fehmarn Belt, 1983</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;Tensions are rising between NATO and Warsaw Pact. There are indications that United Baltic Fleets consisting of Soviet, Polisch and&amp;nbsp;East-Germany (GDR) naval forces could&amp;nbsp;plan an amphibious assault on Danish and West-German (FRG) beaches to get control over Danish Straits and Baltic Approaches (BALTAP).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;NATO&amp;nbsp;plans for mining the Fehmarn Belt area (and some Danish sounds) as preparation for an upcoming hostilities. Only the Oeresund between Denmark and Sweden should&amp;nbsp;remain open for international shipping meanwhile.&lt;BR&gt;These plans were subject to diplomatic negotiations. USSR protested against the mining of Fehmarn Belt and&amp;nbsp;insist on&amp;nbsp;free navigation through Fehmarn Belt and Great Belt to the North Sea.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You are commanding a Task Force consisting of German (FRG) forces with Danish support for mining Fehmarn Belt and Fehmarn Sund. Leave open a narrow shipping lane in the south of&amp;nbsp;Fehmarn Belt for further transit of own naval forces.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;We do not want further escalation of this crisis. Warsaw Pact behaviour is not very aggressive or escalating so far. Only East-German (GDR) and Polish forces operating in the western Baltic. USSR announced that they will react immediately with mine-sweeping missions and&amp;nbsp;send a convoy through Fehmarn Belt and Great Belt to demonstrate their claims on free navigation.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
  <Complexity>2</Complexity>
  <Difficulty>1</Difficulty>
